WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.000
 

00:00:08.360 --> 00:00:09.720
What's good, y'all!

00:00:09.720 --> 00:00:12.440
This week we wising up with Siddhartha, by Herman Hesse.

00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:22.900
Stoner Siddhartha got one thing on his mind, getting so turned up on spiritual enlightenment, that he find legit peace by getting rid of his self.

00:00:22.900 --> 00:00:27.180
Sid been keeping it church as a Brahmin for years, but he just ain't jiving with it.

00:00:27.180 --> 00:00:30.740
I mean if them Brahmins really know it all, why ain't any of them enlightened?

00:00:30.740 --> 00:00:36.500
So Siddhartha and his back-wind brother Govinda decide to join up with a group of Semanas, rolling through the hood.

00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:37.000
 

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:46.860
These cats get they sacred on by denying themselves food, swag, and even poontang, all so they can empty themselves from everything, thirst, sadness, even joy.

00:00:46.860 --> 00:00:53.780
But after a while, Siddhartha and Govinda realize that Samana grind ain't giving them the spiritual juice they jonesin for.

00:00:53.780 --> 00:01:01.400
So when he and Govinda get word that there be some bruh named Buddha, who got the enlightenment game sowed up, they decide to slide over to his spot.

00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:03.840
Govinda really diggin' his Buddhism swagga,

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:07.440
but Siddhartha start thinkin' dat ain't nobody can teach a brutha enlightenment

00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:09.900
no mata' how much street cred yo' teacha get.

00:01:09.900 --> 00:01:12.140
It's a personal thang, naw I mean?

00:01:12.140 --> 00:01:14.780
Govinda stayed, but Siddhartha hop up on a ferry

00:01:14.780 --> 00:01:17.440
to experience a new side of life up in the city.

00:01:17.440 --> 00:01:19.860
Sid ain't got the ends to pay this ferryman,

00:01:19.860 --> 00:01:21.560
but brotha say, "No problem, blood.

00:01:21.560 --> 00:01:23.440
You'll hook me up anotha' way."

00:01:23.440 --> 00:01:25.500
When Sid hits the mean streets of the city,

00:01:25.500 --> 00:01:28.040
he peep game at a dime named Kamala(?).

00:01:28.040 --> 00:01:29.600
She teach 'im how to love

00:01:29.600 --> 00:01:32.800
but only after he get rich, of course. New money!

00:01:32.800 --> 00:01:34.900
but nonna tha' booze, booty, and dice of da world

00:01:34.900 --> 00:01:37.160
can give a brotha da answers he itchin' fo'.

00:01:37.160 --> 00:01:39.460
Matta' fact, it only make it worse!

00:01:39.460 --> 00:01:42.140
[It's] so bad, that Sid thinkin' of snuffin' it.

00:01:42.140 --> 00:01:45.220
So Siddhartha go back to the ferryman, [who's named] Vasudeva,

00:01:45.220 --> 00:01:46.720
seekin' sum legit wisdom.

00:01:46.720 --> 00:01:49.260
Fool say he found inner peace not from religion,

00:01:49.260 --> 00:01:51.460
not from banging honeys and sipping Henney,

00:01:51.620 --> 00:01:52.820
but from da river.

00:01:52.820 --> 00:01:55.380
Then one day that dame Kamala up and died,

00:01:55.380 --> 00:01:57.420
leavin' her little sh*t son with her baby daddy,

00:01:57.420 --> 00:01:59.400
who turn out ta be Siddhartha!

00:01:59.480 --> 00:02:00.920
Gotta wrap it up, Sid!

00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:03.040
Any enlightened brutha' knows that.

00:02:03.040 --> 00:02:04.660
Siddhartha tried to look after him,

00:02:04.660 --> 00:02:05.740
but this kid such a hater,

00:02:05.740 --> 00:02:07.920
that he eventually boosts all dat cash,

00:02:07.920 --> 00:02:09.520
and bounces out of the city!

00:02:09.520 --> 00:02:11.740
Siddhartha tried to catch him, but then he realized,

00:02:11.740 --> 00:02:15.260
"Sh*t, I gotta let him go so he can figure out life fo' himself."

00:02:15.260 --> 00:02:17.240
Afta studyin' da river for years,

00:02:17.240 --> 00:02:21.240
Siddhartha finally recognize da oneness and timelessness of the universe.

00:02:21.740 --> 00:02:24.460
All things and all people are all connected,

00:02:24.460 --> 00:02:26.160
like part of one big-*ss river!

00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:28.880
There ain't no past, present, or future neither,

00:02:28.880 --> 00:02:30.720
'cause time is just manmade.

00:02:30.720 --> 00:02:32.300
Straight-up enlightened, yo.

00:02:32.460 --> 00:02:34.620
Then Vasudeva goes to the forest

00:02:34.620 --> 00:02:36.740
where he gonna chill for the rest of his days,

00:02:36.740 --> 00:02:40.140
and Siddhartha start rockin' the ferryman game solo.

00:02:40.140 --> 00:02:42.920
Years later, homeboy Govinda comes to the river.

00:02:42.920 --> 00:02:44.420
He don't recognize Siddhartha at first,

00:02:44.420 --> 00:02:45.280
but he all like,

00:02:46.480 --> 00:02:47.680
Siddhartha like,

00:02:47.680 --> 00:02:52.040
"Look playa, I can give ya knowledge, but true-blue wisdom can't be said."

00:02:52.040 --> 00:02:54.920
At first, Govinda like, "You holdin' out on me, dawg?"

00:02:54.920 --> 00:02:57.140
When Sid realizes that words ain't cuttin' it,

00:02:57.140 --> 00:02:59.040
he gotta move to the language of the universe:

00:02:59.240 --> 00:02:59.740
love.

00:02:59.740 --> 00:03:01.900
So he tellin' Govinda to give him a kiss on the forehead.

00:03:02.680 --> 00:03:05.000
BAM! Instant enlightenment, man.

00:03:08.100 --> 00:03:11.060
Peeps were all about this book in the late 1950s,

00:03:11.060 --> 00:03:13.860
'specially American kids lookin' for meaning.

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:17.540
they were all up on Hesse's junk sayin' this book got da answers to life's craziness.

00:03:17.540 --> 00:03:20.900
Now, don't pay no mind to the book being split into two parts.

00:03:20.900 --> 00:03:23.660
It's better to look at it like it's divided into three.

00:03:23.660 --> 00:03:24.560
In the first section,

00:03:24.560 --> 00:03:27.400
Old Siddy try to get wise by living the life of the mind.

00:03:27.400 --> 00:03:30.140
When dat don't work, he moved on to the life of the flesh.

00:03:30.680 --> 00:03:34.120
On sipping drank, blowing dank, blowing cash fast,

00:03:34.120 --> 00:03:35.220
and gettin' BOOTAY!

00:03:35.220 --> 00:03:37.280
And neither one gettin' him legit wisdom.

00:03:37.280 --> 00:03:40.140
Only by bringing all dat life's suffering together

00:03:40.140 --> 00:03:43.120
is he able to reach enlightenment by listenin' to da river.

00:03:43.120 --> 00:03:44.880
And that's Hesse's main jam.

00:03:44.880 --> 00:03:48.160
Like Siddhartha say, "Wisdom can't be passed on, playa!"

00:03:57.740 --> 00:04:00.800
Enlightenment ain't about listenin' to da right teacher or reading the right book.

00:04:00.800 --> 00:04:02.900
Even if it's a book as dank as this one,

00:04:02.900 --> 00:04:04.600
ya gotta figure it out for yourself.

00:04:04.920 --> 00:04:06.040
Ya gotta live it.

00:04:06.040 --> 00:04:08.140
Like my brother from another mother Nietzsche said,

00:04:22.340 --> 00:04:23.520
So stop listening to me!

00:04:23.640 --> 00:04:26.040
Get yo *ss outta yo chair, and go find yourself.

00:04:26.040 --> 00:04:28.460
But make sure you hit dat Subscribe button first

00:04:28.460 --> 00:04:30.880
and cop some of my sweet Thug Notes swag.

00:04:31.260 --> 00:04:33.500
Catch ya later, my ballas! Peace.

